WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.910
So, Anna, is it hard to make friends in D.C.?

2
00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.490
At first it was hard.

3
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.530
But now, Marsha is a good friend.

4
00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.170
And there’s Pete.

5
00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:21.170
Of all the people I know in D.C., Pete is the most serious and also the silliest.

6
00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.550
He sounds … interesting.

7
00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:30.590
Jonathan and Ashley are two other good friends of mine.

8
00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:34.450
In the city, they are the friendliest people I know.

9
00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.290
They always help me when I need it.

10
00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:39.170
Your friends sound great!

11
00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.710
So, tell me about your job.

12
00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:44.030
I love my work!

13
00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:49.710
I make a children’s show called the “Time Traveling Treehouse.”

14
00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:53.910
Anna, that is the best job for you!

15
00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.070
Do you remember when we were little?

16
00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:04.370
We played in that old treehouse behind my family’s house for hours!

17
00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.150
I forgot about that!

18
00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:10.090
We thought it really time traveled!

19
00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:13.310
It is really good to talk to you.

20
00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:15.370
New friends are good.

21
00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:18.670
But old friends are the best.

22
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:19.910
I know.

23
00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:24.110
Our hometown isn’t the same now.

24
00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:27.230
You are not there.

25
00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:29.130
No crying.

26
00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.390
No crying.

27
00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:37.570
Penelope, why don't you move here and live with me and Marsha?

28
00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:41.130
Anna, I can’t leave our hometown.

29
00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:46.130
You forget -- I love my job, too.

30
00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:48.350
I didn’t forget.

31
00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:52.090
You are the most famous turkey farmer I know!

32
00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:53.570
Thanks, Anna.

33
00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:55.090
Come on.

34
00:01:55.360 --> 00:02:00.170
Let’s go eat dinner at one of D.C.’s most famous restaurants.

35
00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:01.530
Awesome!
